WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:04.590
There's always something coming and going
on Netflix with every new month, but May just

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:06.260
might be one of the best months yet.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:10.480
From a whole bunch of new releases to the
return of fan favorites, here's everything

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:13.220
good coming to Netflix in May 2019.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:18.070
The dark comedy Dead to Me stars Christina
Applegate as a grieving widow named Jen who

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:22.820
attends a support group and meets a woman
named Lucy, played by Bloodline's Linda Cardellini.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.800
The two bond over their shared grief, become
friends, move in together...and everything

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.700
goes completely off the rails.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:35.320
It turns out Lucy's kind of, maybe, totally
crazy, and now she's living in the same house

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:36.940
as Jen and her kids.

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:41.380
The trailer for Dead to Me teases a heartfelt
drama infused with the kind of humor that

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:45.670
could only come from having Will Ferrell and
Adam McKay as executive producers.

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:47.620
Tune in when the series arrives on May 3rd.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.080
The title of this one says it all.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:54.920
Extremely Wicked, Shockingly Evil and Vile
is about the trial and imprisonment of notorious

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:59.360
serial killer Ted Bundy, told through the
perspective of a single mother who dated Bundy

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:01.260
before his crimes came to light.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:03.400
"I'm disguised as an attorney today."

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:08.820
Zac Efron stars as Bundy, with Lilly Collins
in the role of Elizabeth.

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:13.630
Extremely Wicked, Shockingly Evil and Vile
has all the makings of a dark, twisted descent

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:14.950
into the mind of a killer.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:16.760
Take a look when it lands on May 3rd.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.640
Flinch is an upcoming reality show that works
in the same vein as Fear Factor.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:25.600
Contestants are put into gut-wrenching situations
and tasked with not flinching.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:27.940
Whoever flinches the least wins.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:29.220
What kind of stuff are they doing?

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:34.080
In the trailer, we see challenges as simple
as having a firecracker pop next to you or

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:38.549
a guy smashing cymbals right behind your head,
all the way up to seriously flinch-worthy

00:01:38.549 --> 00:01:43.380
situations like being strapped to a chair
while a cement block on a rope swings inches

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:44.540
past your nose.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:48.540
You can squeal in terror when the first season
swings in on May 3rd.

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:53.560
For its first three seasons, Lucifer was the
property of Fox, and Netflix added seasons

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:54.360
after they aired.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:58.950
But now that Fox has dumped the series, Netflix
swooped in to grab the rights, and they produced

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:00.260
the upcoming fourth season.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:02.660
Other than that, nothing much is going to
change.

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:07.320
It's still the story of Lucifer after he gets
bored with hell and moves to L.A. Hell 2.0,

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:08.100
if you will.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:11.300
"Oh, it's times like this I wish I was still
in hell."

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:15.220
The fourth season of Lucifer arrives on May
8th, so keep your eyes peeled for that.

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:21.260
The Society centers on an affluent town in
which everybody except the teenagers mysteriously

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:21.900
vanishes.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.880
It isn't long before they develop their own
rules for survival.

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:28.480
If you aren't with the cool crowd, you might
just end up six feet under.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:32.129
It looks like a cross between Mean Girls and
The Purge, which is the kind of premise you

00:02:32.129 --> 00:02:33.780
never thought you'd look forward to.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:35.780
But now that it's here, well, we're pretty
pumped.

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:39.200
Tune in for Season 1 of The Society when it
drops on May 10th.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:43.660
Wine Country follows a group of friends as
they head into the Napa Valley for a carefully

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:48.640
planned weekend of boozing to celebrate the
50th birthday of Abby, played by Amy Poehler.

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:53.010
But once all that wine starts stirring around
regrets and repressed emotions, the itinerary

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:57.280
goes out the window and this group of friends
takes a nosedive into a long, hard look at

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:58.000
their lives.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:02:59.000
Fun!

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:03.459
Maya Rudolph, Jason Schwartzman, and Tina
Fey co-star, and Amy Poehler is directing.

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:07.220
Pour a glass and settle in when Wine Country
premieres on May 10th.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:12.060
Even though it's ramping into its second season,
a lot of Netflix viewers have probably never

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:13.040
heard of White Gold.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:17.270
The show centers on a team of salesmen in
a showroom in the '80s who think "business

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:21.350
ethics" is just a fancy phrase for making
as much money as possible, no matter what

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:22.040
it takes.

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:25.820
If you're looking for a new comedy series
to binge, be sure to check out White Gold

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:28.280
when the second season lands on May 17th.

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:33.080
The first season of the Danish thriller series
The Rain was praised by critics for its writing

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:34.100
and characters.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:38.500
It's about a group of people banding together
to survive after a rain-borne plague wipes

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:39.820
out most of humanity.

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:44.000
The series centers on two siblings who leave
their bunker to find other survivors.

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:47.720
If you missed the first season of The Rain,
queue it up and get ready for the second season

00:03:47.739 --> 00:03:48.989
to fall on May 17.

00:03:49.989 --> 00:03:54.150
Spike Lee is producing this time travel joint,
which sees two high school kids on the cusp

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:58.740
of finishing a pair of time warping backpacks
when one of their brothers is shot by police.

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:02.820
They decide to use the backpacks to go back
in time and stop the incident from taking

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:03.320
place.

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:07.420
Of course, things go wrong pretty quickly,
and they find themselves in a loop of mistakes

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:09.670
that they desperately try to unravel.

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:12.040
Apparently, time travel isn't as easy as it
looks.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:15.540
Jump in for the ride when See You Yesterday
shows up on May 17th.

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:20.860
Netflix's horror series Slasher brought in
solid reviews on its first outing thanks mostly

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:22.660
to its dedication to the genre.

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:26.980
Structured on the slasher movies of the '80s
and '90s, it manages to pay tribute to those

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:29.780
films while still bringing plenty of new stuff
to the table.

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:34.060
The newest installment, Solstice, isn't coming
with a lot of pre-release details.

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:38.220
All we know is that if it's anything like
the first two installments, we're 100 percent

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:38.720
in.

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:40.240
Take a look on May 23rd.

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:44.960
Netflix has been adding some pretty twisted
high concept horror lately with releases like

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:50.260
Velvet Buzzsaw and Await Further Instructions,
and continuing that trend in May is The Perfection.

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:55.120
Allison Williams of Get Out stars as a musical
prodigy who returns to her roots at her former

00:04:55.139 --> 00:04:59.240
school, only to get an unexpected surprise
in the form of a younger student who appears

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:00.440
to be deeply disturbed.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:04.320
There aren't many details available for the
rest of the plot, and most reviewers have

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:07.880
stressed how important it is to go into The
Perfection completely blind.

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:11.680
We're looking forward to doing just that when
The Perfection drops on May 24th.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:16.870
How to Sell Hugs Online (Fast) is based on
a ridiculous true story about a teenager in

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:21.839
Germany who was trying to show his girlfriend
how cool he was, so he made a little business

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.600
selling drugs over the internet.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:27.280
Before long, he was one of the top drug dealers
on the continent.

00:05:27.289 --> 00:05:31.839
As the title suggests, How to Sell Hugs Online
(Fast) plays as sort of a dramatic guide to

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:33.020
everything this kid did.

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:35.440
You can find it on Netflix on May 31st.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:40.220
Heart-wrenching and dramatic, When They See
Us is a limited series focused on the Central

00:05:40.229 --> 00:05:44.580
Park Five, five teens who were falsely convicted
of assaulting a woman in New York's Central

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:46.100
Park in 1989.

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:51.400
After spending years in prison, their convictions
were overturned in 2002 in light of new evidence

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:52.920
confirming their innocence.

00:05:53.309 --> 00:05:57.320
When They See Us will paint a dramatic portrait
of the young men's lives before and after

00:05:57.320 --> 00:06:00.240
the crime, and the discrimination they faced
during the trial.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:01.900
Look for it on May 31st.

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:05.200
Those are all the best Netflix originals coming
in May.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:06.780
Now let's look at everything else.

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:12.500
Explosions, kung fu, and space dinosaurs fill
out the docket for May's action additions.

00:06:12.509 --> 00:06:16.370
On May 1st, all three of the Matrix films
plug into the streaming service.

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:18.319
In the mood for more thoughtful fare?

00:06:18.319 --> 00:06:23.569
Check out Snowpiercer, a 2013 post-apocalyptic
film starring Chris Evans as a lowly citizen

00:06:23.569 --> 00:06:26.680
onboard a train carrying the last remnants
of humanity.

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:31.220
There's also going to be a wide range of thriller
and horror films landing on Netflix next month,

00:06:31.229 --> 00:06:35.330
from movies like The Final Destination and
Scream to more low-key adventure thrillers

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:38.280
like The Da Vinci Code and its sequel, Angels
&amp; Demons.

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:40.800
All of those selections arrive on the first
of the month.

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:46.379
Also on the first, look for dramas like Hoosiers,
Scarface, and Revolutionary Road, not to mention

00:06:46.379 --> 00:06:49.539
the mind-bending cult classic Fear and Loathing
in Las Vegas.

00:06:49.539 --> 00:06:54.430
Then, on the fourth, don't miss War Horse,
Steven Spielberg's 2011 World War I drama

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:57.580
that will turn you into a horse lover whether
you want to be one or not.

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:02.120
If you find yourself on the credits-end of
Revolutionary Road come May 1 and desperately

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:04.680
need a pick-me-up, you'll have plenty of options.

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:09.020
Netflix is doubling down on comedies next
month, bringing back raunchy genre favorites

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:13.800
like the first two Austin Powers films, Dumb
and Dumber, Harold &amp; Kumar Escape from Guantanamo

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:15.619
Bay, and Wedding Crashers.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:16.760
Look for those on the first.

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:19.820
Fans of CW superheroes rejoice!

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:23.939
Netflix is adding new seasons of the hottest
superhero shows throughout the month, promising

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:26.520
all the spandex and CGI you could ever want.

00:07:26.789 --> 00:07:32.139
Arrow shows up on the 21st, The Flash on the
22nd, and Season 4 of both Supergirl and Legends

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:33.480
of Tomorrow on the 31st.

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:37.880
And if you've spent the last decade and a
half following the adventures of Sam and Dean

00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:42.040
Winchester, you'll also be able to catch up
on Season 14 of Supernatural on the 3rd.

00:07:42.050 --> 00:07:46.020
It's a little bittersweet, since fans know
the long-running show will finally be entering

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:48.100
the afterlife after its 15th season.

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:53.740
Other shows to look for include Colony: Season
3 on the 2nd, Pose: Season 1 on the 10th,

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:58.020
Riverdale: Season 3 on the 23rd, and the first
two seasons of Outlander on the 27th.

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:00.419
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:04.100
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
Netflix stuff are coming soon.

00:08:04.229 --> 00:08:07.380
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

